       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.          SRETWVLS.
       AUTHOR.              A LEPERA.
       DATE-WRITTEN.        APRIL, 1983.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      *INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
      *SECURITY.
      *REMARKS.
      *D   THIS IS THE RETURN WITH VALUE SUBPROGRAM
      *
      *    PROGRAM WAS COPIED COMPLETELY FROM TMISCACT ON APRIL 10, 1984.
      *
      *    ON APR 10, 1984, CONTAINS REQ UPDATE CALLING    "TREQFILU"
      *    SUBROUTINE FOR ALL REQFILE LOGIC - IN ACCOUNT SL - RUN MUST
      *    NOW SPECIFY ";LIB=P".
      *                                                               E
      *    ON APR 10, 1984, PROGRAM RUNS ON ANY TERMINAL (ESPECIALLY
      *    2626A).  ADDED TO LOGIC TO DETERMINE TERMINAL TYPE.
      *
      *    ON APR 10, 1984, CONTAINS PARAMETERS FOR CALLING
      *    "TREQFILU".  THE ADDED FIELDS ARE "SAVE-RSRVD-BEFORE"
      *    AND "STR-RESERVED" (RESERVED QTY AFTER THE TRANSACTION).
      *    THIS IS BECAUSE THE REQFILE UPDATE SUBPROGRAM WILL NOW CREATE
      *    AUTO REQS ON THE BASIS OF AVAILABLE RATHER THAN ONHAND.
      *    HOWEVER IN THIS PGM, "STR-RESERVED" IS USED FOR BOTH
      *    RESERVED BEFORE AND RESERVED AFTER PARAMETERS, SINCE THIS
      *    QTY CANNOT CHANGE DURING THE TRANSACTION. (THIS PGM DOES
      *    NOT CHANGE RESERVED, AND THE CODE IS LOCKED DURING THE
      *    TRANSACTION).
      *
      *    ON JANUARY 25, 1985, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *      1.  FINISHED CONVERSION TO VIEW THAT WAS STARTED ON APRIL
      *          10, 1984.  NOTE:  THE PREVIOUS CHANGES WERE NEVER
      *          RELEASED TO THE PLANTS.
      *      2.  ADDED CALLS TO "TTERMTYP" TO DETERMINE TERMINAL TYPE
      **         AND SET VIEW PARAMTERS, "TBLOWUP" TO HANDLE FATAL
      *          ERROR CONDITIONS, "TSHWRDFM" TO HANDLE SHOWFORM,
      *          READFIELDS, AND FUNCTION KEYS, AND "TMTLSTAT" TO
      *          ALLOW MATERIAL STATUS INQUIRY.
      *      3.  A REVERSING TRANSACTION TO THE RETURN WITH VALUE
      *          IS ADDED - IN CASE A MISTAKE IS MADE, A REVERSING
      *          TRANSACTION CAN BE GENERATED.
      *      4.  CALLS TO "DBBEGIN" AND "DBEND" WERE ADDED TO GET
      *          READY FOR TRANSACTION LOGGING.
      *     CIH.
      *
      *    ON MAY 16, 1985, CHANGED THIS SUBPROGRAM FOR THE
      *    EUROPEAN DATE CONVERSION.  IT WILL NOW CALL "TDATECHK"
      *    FOR ALL DATE MANIPULATION, WHICH WILL RESULT IN A
      *    EUROPEAN STLYE DATE ON THE OUTPUT DOCUMENT IF THE
      *    EUROPEAN DATE FLAG IS SET.  CIH.
      *
      *   10/ 8/85  ADDED CALLS TO FINDJCW, NLAPPEND, CATOPEN, AND *
      *             CATCLOSE IN ORDER TO ACCOMODATE THE NATIVE     *
      *             LANGUAGE SUPPORT FACILITY.  ADDED LINKAGES AND *
      *             ALSO MADE THE CHANGE TO THE FORMFILE NAMES.    *
      *             CHANGED ALL REFERENCES OF TSCRPRNT TO TSCRPRT2,*
      *             TDATECHK TO TDATECK2.                          *
      *             THIS WAS TO INCORPORATE THE NATIVE LANGUAGE    *
      *             SUPPORT VERSIONS OF THESE SUBROUTINES.         *
      *                                           PD RAGLOW.       *
      **************************************************************
      *
      *    06/17/86.
      *      REPLACED CALL TO "TFDESC" WITH CALL TO "CDESC".  "CDESC"
      *      HAS MORE OPTIONS, AND HANDLES THE DATA SETS "DMANPART" - USING
      *      THE MANUFACTURER ENTRIES AS PART OF DESCRIPTION. CIH.
      *
      *      JUNE 27, 1986                C.R. KALMAN
      *         1. HARD-CODED ESCAPE SEQUENCES REMOVED FROM
      *            PROGRAM.  THEY ARE NOW TO BE EXTERNALLY
      *            SUPPLIED.
      *         2. THE MAIN PROGRAM IN A JOB STREAM WILL
      *            COPY ESC-NAM2 THAT CONTAINS THE HP
      *            ESCAPE SEQUENCES.  IT WILL ALSO CALL
      *            TESCSEQ THAT CONTAINS THE NON-HP ESCAPE
      *            SEQUENCES, IF ANY ARE USED.  THE NON-HP
      *            SEQUENCES WILL OVERRIDE THE HP SEQUENCES.
      *         3. THE ACTUAL PRINTING PROGRAM WILL GET THE
      *            APPROPRIATE SEQUENCES PASSED DOWN TO IT
      *            THRU THE INTERMEDIATE SUBROUTINES THAT
      *            COPY ESC-NAME.
      *C
      *C 01-19-93    BK DISMUKES    NAPANEE CONV
      *C    CHANGED
      *C        SELECT ONLINE-PRT ASSIGN TO PRINTER-CSISPRT.
      *C    TO READ
      *C        SELECT ONLINE-PRT ASSIGN TO PRINTER-MCPRT.
      *C    SO IT WOULD BE STANDARD WITH OTHER PROGRAMS.
      *C
      *C 07MAY1996   DAVE PLUM      REQUEST #6598
      *C    1) ADDED COMPANY CODE TO THE SET OF PARAMETERS
      *C       BEING RECEIVED FROM THE CALLING PROGRAM TUDCSTR.
      *C    2) ADDED COMPANY CODE TO THE SET OF PARAMETERS
      *C       BEING PASSED TO SUBROUTINE CISITRAW.
      *C
      *C 06/12/96    JEFF BUNGO
      *C    EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C    INCLUDE CENTURY ON STORE ACTIVITY DATE.
      *C
      *C 06/13/96    JEFF BUNGO
      *C    REMOVE COMPRESSED AND UNDERLINE PRINTING IN DOCUMENT.
      *C
      *C 05/12/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C    ADD EDIT TO RETURN ONLY TO GOODYEAR BINS
      *C
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       SPECIAL-NAMES. C01 IS NEW-PAGE.

       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT ONLINE-PRT ASSIGN TO PRINTER-MCPRT.

           SELECT DDAILYTC
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1601
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                    WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MSTORERM-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MSTORERM-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MVALIDPLTDATA
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1701
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MPLTINFO
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.

       FD  ONLINE-PRT
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 132 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS PRINT-RCD.
       01  PRINT-RCD.
           05  PRINT-LINE                PIC X(132).

       FD  DDAILYTC
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DDAILYTC-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS1600  OF MCFLCS1601.

       FD  MSTORERM-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSTORERM-I-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0200  OF MCFLCS0201.

       FD  MSTORERM-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSTORERM-O-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0200  OF MCFLCS0201.

       FD  MVALIDPLTDATA
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MVALIDPLTDATA-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS1700  OF MCFLCS1701.

       FD  MPLTINFO
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MPLTINFO-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0500  OF MCFLCS0501.

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

       77  SUB                           PIC 9(1)   VALUE 0.
       77  LOC-COUNT                     PIC 9(1)   VALUE 0.
       77  TOTAL-QTY                     PIC S9(8)  VALUE ZEROS.
       77  SAVE-PARA-NUMBER              PIC 9(2)  VALUE 0.

      *****ARGUMENT VALUES*****
       77  CODE-ARG                      PIC X(8)   VALUE SPACES.

      *****D-E IS THE LINE OF DE BEING WORKED ON*****
       77  D-E                           PIC 99     VALUE ZEROS.

       77  LINE-ADV                      PIC 99     VALUE ZEROS.
       77  ADD-LOC-SW                    PIC X      VALUE "N".
       77  FIRST-TIME-FLAG               PIC X(1)   VALUE "Y".
       77  PRT-CODE-FLAG                 PIC X(1)   VALUE "N".
       77  SAVE-ONHAND-BEFORE            PIC S9(8)  VALUE 0.
       77  SAVE-RSRVD-BEFORE             PIC S9(8)  VALUE 0.
       77  REQFILNO                      PIC S9(4) COMP  VALUE 0.
       77  RET-CODE                      PIC X(2)  VALUE "01".
       77  DUMMY-CODE-PARM               PIC X(7)  VALUE SPACES.

